WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:06.160
If you want to see a tragic preview, really,
of the voter suppression and catastrophic

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.559
disenfranchisement that we're going to see
in the November election.

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:14.240
Look no further than yesterday in Georgia.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.640
Georgia, among some other states, had primary
elections yesterday.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.530
And you may or may not even have heard that
elections were going on in local elections,

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.689
depending on what media sources you consume.

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:29.859
You may not even have been aware that there
were problems or that there were even elections

00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:31.289
yesterday, but there were.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:37.420
And this is really, truly a crisis level situation
where the United States looks much more like

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:42.260
the developing countries that are right wing
leaders often criticize.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:47.839
Based on what our elections looked like yesterday,
we had people waiting in lines, hours and

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:53.940
hours long, outdoors in the heat, often wearing
masks because we are still, by the way, dealing

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.479
with the corona virus pandemic.

00:00:55.479 --> 00:01:01.459
Of course, this was there were shortages of
ballots and this was all disproportionately

00:01:01.459 --> 00:01:09.020
in the minority precincts, parts of the state
of Georgia, where the population is majority,

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:14.969
minority places that tend on average to vote
more for Democrats than they tend to vote

00:01:14.969 --> 00:01:16.549
for Republicans.

00:01:16.549 --> 00:01:20.119
And at some point, I mean, how many times
are we going to see the exact same story?

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:22.400
And the answer is probably many, sadly.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.310
But we've been watching this four election
cycle after election cycle.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:29.750
This happened back in Georgia back in 2018
in Georgia.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.070
That was one separate.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:36.780
Then Secretary of State Brian Kemp, a Republican,
was running for governor.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:42.100
And as secretary of state, he oversaw his
own election.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.319
Again, Stacey Abrams to be governor of Georgia.

00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:52.820
Ultimately, one big surprise and widespread
allegations of the exact same type of voter

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:58.109
suppression, disenfranchisement, reduction
of polling places in disproportionately minority

00:01:58.109 --> 00:01:59.689
and Democratic leaning areas.

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:00.689
It's the same game.

00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:05.920
And the reason that Republicans are going
to aggressively push this in Georgia is that

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.970
Georgia is increasingly a contested state.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:14.730
Now, I don't want to pretend like it's a battleground
state in any real sense right now presidentially.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:20.870
For now, it's still a state that Trump is
likely going to win modestly, easily.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:25.820
He's up in the polls about seven points right
now in Georgia.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.430
He'll almost certainly win.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:33.620
But the point is Georgia in local and state
elections is increasingly purple.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:38.599
It's close enough for Trump that he's going
to have to spend some money there, which is

00:02:38.599 --> 00:02:41.130
money he can't spend in two places.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.790
He's going to spend it there instead of somewhere
else.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:47.740
Back in 2016, Donald Trump only won Georgia
by five percentage points.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:53.240
In the 2012 election, Mitt Romney had defeated
Barack Obama by eight in Georgia.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:58.800
And again, it's the state and local races
are maybe suggestive of what we might see

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.430
in the future in Georgia, which is more of
a centrist lean than a hard right lean.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.860
And Republicans are understandably very worried.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.780
So we saw a preview yesterday in Georgia of
what we're going to see in a ton of places

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:11.849
in the fall.

00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:14.310
This includes Florida, Ohio, Wisconsin.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:21.640
Really, it's like every contested battleground
state that was important to Trump in 2016

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:25.239
that he can't really afford to lose without
putting his reelection at risk.

00:03:25.239 --> 00:03:28.060
We are going to see this exact same thing.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:34.010
Now, of course, lots of Georgia voters, you'll
be glad to know, had no problem at all voting

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.180
yesterday.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:41.790
Voters who disproportionately vote in overwhelmingly
white precincts and they were widely reporting.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.250
Listen, I showed up and voted in five minutes.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.250
There was no line.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.469
What are people complaining about?

00:03:46.469 --> 00:03:48.099
And that's exactly the strategy.

00:03:48.099 --> 00:03:53.200
Make it really easy for voters that are statistically
more likely to vote Republican to vote.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:58.010
Make it much more difficult for voters that
at the aggregate, you know, broad mathematical

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.859
level are more likely to vote for Democrats.

00:04:00.859 --> 00:04:05.830
And it's the same betrayal of Georgia voters
once again.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.159
This is election rigging.

00:04:07.159 --> 00:04:14.209
We have to stop using these softer terms like
there were reports of isolated irregularities.

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:16.350
Come on.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:20.950
There were delays voting in some precincts.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:23.670
Those are essentially gaslighting terms.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:26.470
This is rigging because it's intentional.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.480
It's calculated.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:34.040
It's an effort to swing results by controlling
and manipulating and sort of molding who gets

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.510
to vote easily versus who's going to have
trouble voting.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.250
So a few things have to happen.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:46.770
First, we need as many nonprofit groups as
possible to be armed and ready to fight every

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:52.210
voter suppression attempt when they try to
reduce polling places, cut early voting hours,

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:57.580
put stricter guidelines for requesting an
absentee ballot purge voter rolls, as we've

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.610
seen done in a number of different states.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:06.370
We need these nonprofit groups suing every
single time and gumming up any of these attempts

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.760
as much as possible.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:08.760
That's number one.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:14.200
Number two, anybody who can either vote early
or vote absentee should plan to vote early

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:17.790
and or vote absentee and should understand
what the process looks like.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:25.390
Now, in some places, you will have access
to both an absentee ballot vote by mail and

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.470
early voting.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.710
You will have your choice of the two.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:33.020
In some places, it's one or the other, depending
on the absentee ballot rules or the early

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.020
voting rules.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:40.190
So inform yourself about what is going on,
where you vote, the absentee ballot, you request

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.900
from the state ahead of time.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.940
Some states are saying because of corona virus,
they'll send everybody an application for

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.350
an absentee ballot.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.400
Others are looking at sending the ballots
themselves.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:55.350
But the point is, the normal processes, you
request the ballot, you get it, you fill it

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:56.350
out, you mail it in.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:57.350
That's it.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:58.350
You're done.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.350
OK.

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:01.420
Early voting is in-person voting depending
on the state.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:06.290
Sometimes about three weeks before the Election
Day, in this case, November 3rd, early voting

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:07.290
will start.

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.970
It's usually limited locations like here in
Boston.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:12.460
If I want to vote early, I can't vote in my
neighborhood.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:16.540
I have to go to one of I think it's like five
or six locations, including City Hall all

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.190
the way downtown.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.700
Find out where that is.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:24.390
As many people as possible should take advantage
of whichever method is available in their

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:26.150
state and whatever is easier for you.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.890
Now, one last thing.

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:31.900
The Georgia secretary of state says there
is going to be an investigation into what

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:32.900
happened yesterday.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.480
Now, I really want you to understand how absurd
this is.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:42.680
Brian Kemp was secretary of state in November
of 2018, and he ran the election in which

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:44.400
he was a candidate for governor.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.200
And lo and behold, he won amidst allegations
of voter suppression.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:54.570
Now, another secretary of state is going to
investigate voter suppression that he presided

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.280
over to help his own party.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.280
It's a joke.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:06:59.280
We are a joke.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:03.890
It's got a bunch of e-mails yesterday and
today from European viewers saying what's

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:06.330
going on in the U.S. with your voting system?

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:07.690
How is this still a problem?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.560
And one of the richest countries in the world.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.540
And the answer is it's a problem by design.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:15.610
We could solve this, but there isn't a problem.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:20.440
If you ask the people that benefit from this
voter suppression, there are now calls.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.360
It's just unbelievable.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:30.000
There are calls for the U.S. to bring in United
Nations elections observers in November to

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.320
try to ensure that there are fair elections
in the United States.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:38.010
This is how unreliable and pathetic our election
system is.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:08:50.170
And we're going to see a lot more of it as
we get closer and closer

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:53.220
to November.

